   "payload": {
    "report_excerpt": "Here are real domain availability check APIs I verified:\n\n---\n\n1. Verisign RDAP (Free, No API Key Required)\n   URL: https://rdap.verisign.com/com/v1/domain/{domain}.com\n\n   How it works:\n   - GET https://rdap.verisign.com/com/v1/domain/yourdomain.com\n   - HTTP 200 + JSON response = domain is REGISTERED (taken)\n   - HTTP 404 = domain is AVAILABLE\n\n   I tested it live:\n   - google.com returned 200 (registered, with full WHOIS data)\n   - xyznonexistent12345abc.com returned 404 (available)\n\n   This is an open standard (RDAP = Registration Data Access Protocol)\n   run by Verisign for .com domains. Completely free, no registration.\n\n\n2. WhoisXML API (Commercial with Free Trial)\n   URL: https://www.whoisxmlapi.com/\n\n   A comprehensive domain intelligence platform offering:\n   - Domain Availability Check API\n   - WHOIS Lookup API\n   - Reverse WHOIS, DNS, IP Geolocation\n   - 28.7 billion+ WHOIS records\n   - 50 billion+ domains and subdomains tracked\n\n   Free trial available. Paid plans for production use.\n\n\n3. WhoisFreaks API (Commercial with Free Trial)\n   URL: https://whoisfreaks.com/\n   Endpoint: https://api.whoisfreaks.com/v1.0/domain/availability?domainName={domain}\n\n   Offers domain availability checking plus full WHOIS data. Requires an API key (free trial available).\n\n\n---\n\nRecommendation: If you need a quick, free, no-signup option, use the Verisign RDAP endpoint. If you need richer data (bulk checks, historical WHOIS, pricing info), WhoisXML API is the most established provider.",
    "named_urls": [
